# Monetary Anchor – 120% Gold Over-Collateralisation

## Purpose
To provide a hard, verifiable floor for the settlement system and protect against hyperinflation and pure speculative collapse.

## Core Rule
The circulating digital value represented in the system is targeted to be backed by **120% physical gold** (or equivalent allocated gold claims under independent custody).

This means for every 100 units of digital value in circulation, there should be at least 120 units of value held in physical gold reserves.

## Why 120%
- Creates a mathematical buffer above full backing
- Absorbs operational costs, custody fees, and minor discrepancies
- Makes the system more resistant to sudden redemption pressure
- Signals serious long-term monetary intent rather than fractional promises

## How It Fits YOD4COINS

| Historical Gold Standard Problem      | YOD4COINS Structural Response                          |
|---------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------|
| Governments lied about reserves       | Transparent on-chain / protocol-level reporting + independent audits |
| Easy over-issuance                    | Supply rules + collateralisation floor enforced in protocol logic |
| Slow physical transport               | Local offline finality — ownership moves digitally, gold stays vaulted |
| No automatic funding of the system    | 0.1% protocol fee provides continuous operational funding |

## Offline Operation & Proof of Reserves

Full real-time cryptographic verification of physical vault reserves while nodes are completely offline is not possible in the strict sense (physical gold cannot be cryptographically proven without some trusted or semi-trusted oracle/custody layer).

Practical design approach:
- **Normal & Partitioned modes**: Edge nodes can carry recent, signed Proof-of-Reserve attestations.
- **Extreme mode (1f+1)**: Nodes operate on the last known valid collateralisation state and hard local limits. Full reserve verification resumes on reconciliation.
- Periodic independent audits + cryptographic attestations from custodians form the bridge between physical gold and the digital system.

This keeps the offline-first property while still anchoring the system to a hard asset.

## Status
This is an architectural monetary layer. Implementation requires:
- Legal custody arrangements
- Independent auditing
- Clear redemption / issuance rules
- Integration with the existing fee and supply logic

It is designed as a long-term stability upgrade once the core offline settlement protocol has real usage and revenue.
